# Cloudflare Pages reads this from dist/ (like public/_redirects).
#
# The widget is embedded in OTHER sites, so everything it loads at runtime is a
# cross-origin request from the host page's point of view. Fonts are the strict case:
# a font is always fetched in CORS mode, so a missing Access-Control-Allow-Origin
# means the self-hosted Raleway silently fails to render (issue #91).
#
# Pages already serves static assets with `access-control-allow-origin: *`; this pins
# that rather than leaving a rendering requirement on a platform default. Hashed,
# immutable build assets, so the long cache is safe — a change ships under a new URL.
# Everything Vite emits under /assets/ is content-hashed, so the long immutable cache is
# safe — a change ships under a new URL. `embed.js` deliberately sits outside this rule at
# the dist root: it is the one stable URL hosts hardcode, and it must stay revalidated.
/assets/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The locale JSON is fetched cross-origin from every host page (src/config/i18n.ts builds
# the URL from VITE_HOST), and it needs CORS for the same reason the font does — with a
# worse failure: a blocked font degrades to the system sans, blocked locales render every
# string as its raw key. Hand-edited and unhashed, so no long cache.
/locales/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

# Resist direct indexing of this deployment (issue #106) — search is owned by WeMeditate
# and the other embedding sites, and every canonical this build emits already points at
# SahajCloud's `webUrl`. See public/robots.txt for the whole picture; this is the half a
# crawler reads once it has the response in hand.
#
# It is a HEADER as well as index.html's <meta> because the meta only covers documents:
# `_redirects` rewrites every unknown path to index.html, so the meta does cover every
# ROUTE, but not embed.js, the hashed assets or the locale JSON, each of which is a
# fetchable URL of its own. The header covers all of them.
#
# `/*` does not disturb the two rules above: Cloudflare Pages applies EVERY matching
# rule ("an incoming request which matches multiple rules' URL patterns will inherit all
# rules' headers"), so /assets/* keeps its CORS + immutable cache and additionally gets
# this. Ordered last only for reading — combination is not order-sensitive.
#
# This cannot leak into a host page's own indexing: X-Robots-Tag governs the URL it is
# served on, and a directive on a subresource says nothing about the document embedding
# it. `noindex` alone, deliberately — no `nofollow`, because the canonicals point at
# WeMeditate and there is no reason to stop a crawler following them there.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
